# The Vercel deployment is the STATIC dashboard (outputDirectory: dashboard) plus the
# Node functions in api/ (today: api/screen-builder.js, the AI screen builder). Keep the
# Python engine, data, and tooling out of the upload so Vercel never tries to build
# Python. Do NOT add api/ or dashboard/ here: api/screen-builder.js requires
# dashboard/screen-dsl.js and dashboard/screen_fields.json at runtime
# (scripts/test_screen_builder.js checks this file). dashboard/reports/*.json are the Key
# reports, served as static files (scripts/test_reports.js checks they stay in, with real
# gitignore matching). The root-level directories are ANCHORED with a leading slash: a bare
# "data/" matches a directory named data at any depth, which would drop
# dashboard/reports/data/ (the EDGAR financials behind each report, public domain).
/engine/
/scripts/
/data/
/tests/
/supabase/
/.github/
/.venv/
__pycache__/
requirements.txt
.env
.env.*
*.db
*.log
README.md
